ORIGIN

  https://rubygems.org/downloads/racc-1.8.1.gem
  sha256 4a7f6929691dbec8b5209a0b373bc2614882b55fc5d2e447a21aaa691303d62f

  Byte-identical to the copy Ruby 4.0.6 already ships under
  third_party/ruby/.bundle/gems/racc-1.8.1 (verified with diff -r).

WHY IT IS HERE

  Before this directory existed, the xml-libs branch copied only
  racc/parser.rb and racc/info.rb onto the plain load path, as a stopgap so
  nokogiri's generated CSS parser could load.  `require "racc"`, the racc
  *generator*, and any Bundler dependency on racc all still failed, and the
  parse engine was the slow pure-Ruby one.  This vendoring replaces that:
  the whole gem, a real default gemspec, and the cparse C runtime linked in.

LOCAL CHANGES

  - ext/racc/cparse/{cparse.c,extconf.rb} -> cparse/ (unmodified)
  - lib/**                                -> lib/ (unmodified)
  - COPYING, BSDL                         -> here
  - extconf.rb is kept for reference only; its single -D
    (RACC_INFO_VERSION) is hand transcribed into BUILD.mk.
  - racc.gemspec is hand-written (upstream's declares `extensions`).
  - bin/racc, doc/ and the test suite are not vendored; bin/racc is already
    copied into /zip/bin by assemble_stdlib.sh from .bundle/gems.

  No .c or .h file has been modified.
